adjudication.rationale:
In the new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the auth check is:

```ts
if (
  req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
  process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is not set in the runtime environment (so `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET === undefined`) and the request omits the header (so the indexed `req.headers[...]` is also `undefined`), then the comparison becomes `undefined !== undefined`, which is `false`, so the request is incorrectly accepted. Since the handler then allows writing credentials for an arbitrary `userId`, this is a real fail-open authentication bug in the diff. Reachability also depends on `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED`, which is not shown here, but the fail-open logic in the secret check itself is directly verifiable from the diff.
